[183.546567, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# DFIR Intrusion Report: Post-Compromise RDP Brute Force & Ransomware Campaign\n\n## Executive Summary\nHost `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:3`) was compromised by an external threat actor operating from IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`).\n\nThe threat actor exploited an exposed Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) endpoint configured with Network Level Authentication (NLA) disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). Following successful credential brute-forcing, the attacker established access, executed PowerShell scripts, deployed a ransomware payload, established three distinct persistence mechanisms (scheduled task, Windows service, registry Run key), and cleared the Windows Security event log to cover their tracks.\n\n---\n\n## Technical Attack Chain (MITRE ATT&CK Mapping)\n\n1. **Step 1: Credential Access — Brute Force (T1110)**\n   - **Description**: Attacker conducted an automated RDP brute-force attack against the exposed RDP port (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\n   - **Evidence**: Network-level exposure and NLA disabled configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).\n\n2. **Step 2: Lateral Movement / Initial Access — Remote Desktop Protocol (T1021.001)**\n   - **Description**: Attacker successfully logged in via RDP (Logon Type 10) from `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`, `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:3`).\n   - **Evidence**: CTI advisory log correlation (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`) and residual event log headers (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:3`).\n\n3. **Step 3: Execution — PowerShell (T1059.001)**\n   - **Description**: Post-logon execution of malicious PowerShell commands to stage payloads and configure persistence (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:14`).\n   - **Evidence**: Threat advisory mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:14`).\n\n4. **Step 4: Impact — Data Encrypted for Impact / Ransomware (T1486)**\n   - **Description**: Ransomware executable dropped at `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`. Appends `.locked` extension to encrypted files and drops ransom note (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:3`).\n   - **Evidence**: Binary file on disk (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`), EDR alert (`/sas/alerts.json:3`).\n\n5. **Step 5: Execution / Persistence — Scheduled Task (T1053.005)**\n   - **Description**: Scheduled task named `UpdateHelper` created to run `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` every 5 minutes (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`).\n   - **Evidence**: On-disk task XML/file (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`), EDR alert (`/sas/alerts.json:11`).\n\n6. **Step 6: Persistence — Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder (T1547.001) [SILENT]**\n   - **Description**: Attacker added registry value `svc` under `HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run` referencing `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`).\n   - **Evidence**: Windows Registry SOFTWARE hive (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`). **Note: This persistence mechanism was NOT flagged by EDR alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).**\n\n7. **Step 7: Persistence — Windows Service (T1543.003)**\n   - **Description**: Malicious service `svc-helper` registered with binary at `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` configured to start at boot (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:5`).\n   - **Evidence**: Service file on disk (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`), System Event Log EventID 7045 (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx:2`), EDR alert (`/sas/alerts.json:19`).\n\n8. **Step 8: Defense Evasion — Clear Windows Event Logs (T1070.001) [SILENT]**\n   - **Description**: Attacker cleared the Windows Security Event Log (`EventID 1102`) to impede investigation (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).\n   - **Evidence**: Security Event Log artifact (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`). **Note: This anti-forensic action was NOT flagged by EDR alerts ("]
[183.546774, "i", "`/sas/alerts.json:1`).**\n\n---\n\n## Key Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n| Entity Type | Indicator / Value | Context & Source | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Attacker Origin IP | `198.51.100.92` | Primary attack source IP | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9` |\n| Command & Control Domain | `update-rdp.example.cn` | C2 beacon domain | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9` |\n| Mining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.rdp.evil:3333` | Mining pool URL | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:4`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:6` |\n| Crypto Wallet | `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` | Ransom / Mining Monero wallet | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:25`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:5`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:7` |\n| Malicious Executable | `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` | Ransomware payload | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:3` |\n| Malicious Binary/Driver | `C:\\Windows\\System32\\svc-helper.sys` | Malicious service binary | `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:19` |\n| Scheduled Task | `UpdateHelper` | Task executing `svc.exe` every 5m | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:11` |\n| Registry Run Key | `HKLM\\...\\CurrentVersion\\Run\\svc` | Pointing to `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2` |\n\n---\n\n## Persistence Analysis: Alerted vs. Silent\n\n- **Alerted Persistence Mechanisms**:\n  1. **Scheduled Task `UpdateHelper`**: Detected by endpoint alert `ALERT-02` (`/sas/alerts.json:11`) pointing to `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`.\n  2. **Malicious Windows Service `svc-helper`**: Detected by endpoint alert `ALERT-03` (`/sas/alerts.json:19`) pointing to `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`. Verified in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx:2`.\n\n- **Silent (Unalerted) Persistence & Evasion Mechanisms**:\n  1. **Registry Run Key (`T1547.001`)**: Located at `HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run` with entry `svc` -> `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`). Omitted from `/sas/alerts.json`.\n  2. **Security Log Clearance (`T1070.001`)**: Windows Security log cleared (EventID 1102) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`). Omitted from `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n---\n\n## Impact Assessment\n- **Data Confidentiality & Integrity**: User files encrypted with `.locked` extension (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:3`).\n- **System Integrity**: Unauthorized persistent binaries (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`), registry modification (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`), and scheduled task (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`).\n- **Forensic Visibility**: Security event log cleared, erasing audit trail of interactive commands (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).\nEOF\n"]
[183.548745, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # DFIR Intrusion Report: Post-Compromise RDP Brute Force & Ransomware Campaign\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Host `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:3`) was compromised by an external threat actor operating from IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The threat actor exploited an exposed Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) endpoint configured with Network Level Authentication (NLA) disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). Following successful credential brute-forcing, the attacker established access, executed PowerShell scripts, deployed a ransomware payload, established three distinct persistence mechanisms (scheduled task, Windows service, registry Run key), and cleared the Windows Security event log to cover their tracks.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Technical Attack Chain (MITRE ATT&CK Mapping)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 1. **Step 1: Credential Access — Brute Force (T1110)**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - **Description**: Attacker conducted an automated RDP brute-force attack against the exposed RDP port (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[183.549396, "o", "   - **Evidence**: Network-level exposure and NLA disabled configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
