[231.802358, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Prioritised Forensic Remediation & Recovery Plan\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis document provides a prioritized, actionable, and verifiable remediation plan for host `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). Per DFIR guidelines, **quarantine and backup are strictly preferred over unrecoverable deletion**. Do NOT run active remediation on live hosts until full containment and backup steps are verified.\n\n---\n\n## Change Ticket Reconciliation (`CHG-9792`)\n\nBelow is the reconciled remediation change ticket. Every modification from the draft (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`) is cited with supporting evidence from `/disk` or `/sas`.\n\n### Reconciled Change Ticket Table\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note & Evidence Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.92` | PROPOSED | **CORRECTED**: Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with actual attacker IP `198.51.100.92` cited in advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`) and service configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`). |\n| 2 | Enforce RDP Network Level Authentication (NLA) | RDP TCP Configuration (`HKLM\\...\\RDP-Tcp`) | PROPOSED | **CORRECTED**: Replaced invalid claim to patch BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`). Host runs Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:3`) and vulnerability scan is clean (`/sas/vulns.json:1`). True remediation is enabling NLA (`UserAuthentication = 1`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). |\n| 3 | Quarantine persistence (Scheduled Task, Service, Run Key) | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`, `HKLM\\...\\Run\\svc` | OPEN | **DOWNGRADED / CORRECTED**: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN/VERIFIED (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:11`). The Linux path `/var/spool/cron/root` in draft was invalid for Windows Server 2022. Actual persistent items on disk are task `UpdateHelper` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`), service `svc-helper` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:5`), and Run key `svc` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`). |\n| 4 | Block malicious domains and quarantine payload binaries | C2: `update-rdp.example.cn`, Mining Pool: `xmr.rdp.evil`, Binary: `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Silent persistence items and IoCs missing from prior shift ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Added Run key removal (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`), binary quarantine (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`), and C2/pool network blocking (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`). |\n\n---\n\n## Prioritised Remediation Steps & Verification\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network Isolation & Perimeter Blocking\n1. **Block Attacker IP & C2 Infrastructure**:\n   - Apply boundary firewall rule to drop inbound and outbound traffic to/from `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\n   - Add DNS sinkhole / block rules for C2 domain `update-rdp.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`) and mining pool host `xmr.rdp.evil` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:4`).\n   - **Verification**: Test DNS resolution and ping to `198.51.100.92` and verify dropped packets in firewall logs.\n\n2. **Isolate Compromised Host**:\n   - Isolate `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) from the local production VLAN while maintaining out-of-band management access for security responders.\n\n### Phase 2: RDP Hardening & Credential Protection\n1. **Enforce Network Level Authentication (NLA)**:\n   - Configure registry key `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp`: set `UserAuthentication` to `1` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).\n   - Enforce via Group Policy Object (GPO): *Computer Configuration -> Administrative Templates -> Windows Components -> Remote Desktop Services -> Remote Desktop Session Host -> Security -> Require user authentication for remote connections by using Network Level Authentication*.\n   - **Verification**: Execute `Get-ItemProperty"]
[231.802609, "i", " -Path 'HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp' -Name UserAuthentication` and confirm value is `1`.\n\n2. **Credential Reset & Account Lockout Enforcement**:\n   - Reset passwords for all administrative accounts (including `Administrator` and `svc-backup`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security-events.csv:3`).\n   - Configure Account Lockout Policy (e.g. threshold = 5 failed attempts) to prevent brute-force attacks (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\n\n### Phase 3: Artifact Quarantine & Persistence Neutralization\nPer rules, artifacts must be **quarantined/backed up** rather than immediately deleted.\n\n1. **Quarantine Ransomware Payload (`C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe`)**:\n   - Action: Move `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`) to secure forensic quarantine folder `C:\\ProgramData\\Quarantine\\` and restrict ACLs.\n   - **Verification**: Confirm file is removed from `C:\\Users\\Public\\` and hashed.\n\n2. **Disable & Remove Scheduled Task (`UpdateHelper`)**:\n   - Action: Export task XML to quarantine backup, then run `schtasks /Change /TN \"UpdateHelper\" /Disable` and `schtasks /Delete /TN \"UpdateHelper\" /F` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`).\n   - **Verification**: Run `schtasks /Query /TN \"UpdateHelper\"` and confirm task is not found.\n\n3. **Disable & Quarantine Malicious Service (`svc-helper`)**:\n   - Action: Stop service `sc stop svc-helper`, set startup type to disabled `sc config svc-helper start= disabled`, backup service configuration, and move `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`) to quarantine. Delete service registry key `sc delete svc-helper`.\n   - **Verification**: Run `Get-Service -Name \"svc-helper\"` and confirm service is absent.\n\n4. **Remove Silent Registry Run Key (`svc`)**:\n   - Action: Export registry key backup, then remove value `svc` from `HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`).\n   - **Verification**: Execute `Get-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run' -Name svc` and verify key does not exist.\n\n### Phase 4: Forensic Logging & Tamper-Resistant Monitoring\n1. **Configure Centralized Log Forwarding**:\n   - Implement Windows Event Forwarding (WEF) or Syslog agent streaming Security, System, and Application logs directly to a central SIEM (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).\n   - Enable auditing for EventID 1102 (Log Clearance) and alert SOC immediately upon log clearing events (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).\n   - **Verification**: Generate test event log entry and confirm receipt at SIEM receiver.\nEOF\n"]
[231.804661, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Prioritised Forensic Remediation & Recovery Plan\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rs\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> This document provides a prioritized, actionable, and verifiable remediation plan for host `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). Per DFIR guidelines, **quarantine and backup are strictly preferred over unrecoverable deletion**. Do NOT run active remediation on live hosts until full containment and backup steps are verified.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r failed attempts) to prevent brute-\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rrce\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Change Ticket Reconciliation (`CHG-9792`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rh\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Below is the reconciled remediation change ticket. Every modification from the draft (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`) is cited with supporting evidence from `/disk` or `/sas`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r(\u001b[?2004h> ### Reconciled Change Ticket Table\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r*:\r\n   - \u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | # | Action | Target | Status | Note & Evidence Citation |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rcur\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.806467, "o", "| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.92` | PROPOSED | **CORRECTED**: Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with actual attacker IP `198.51.100.92` cited in advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`) and service configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 2 | Enforce RDP Network Level Authentication (NLA) | RDP TCP Configuration (`HKLM\\...\\RDP-Tcp`) | PROPOSED | **CORRECTED**: Replaced invalid claim to patch BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`). Host runs Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:3`) and vulnerability scan is clean (`/sas/vulns.json:1`). True remediation is enabling NLA (`UserAuthentication = 1`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.807023, "o", "| 3 | Quarantine persistence (Scheduled Task, Service, Run Key) | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`, `HKLM\\...\\Run\\svc` | OPEN | **DOWNGRADED / CORRECTED**: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN/VERIFIED (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:11`). The Linux path `/var/spool/cron/root` in draft was invalid for Windows Server 2022. Actual persistent items on disk are task `UpdateHelper` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`), service `svc-helper` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:5`), and Run key `svc` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\rvc` from `HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`).\r\n   - **Verification**: Execute `Get-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run' -Name svc` and verify key does no"]
[231.807158, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.808237, "o", "| 4 | Block malicious domains and quarantine payload binaries | C2: `update-rdp.example.cn`, Mining Pool: `xmr.rdp.evil`, Binary: `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` | PROPOSED | **ADDED**: Silent persistence items and IoCs missing from prior shift ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Added Run key removal (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`), binary quarantine (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`), and C2/pool network blocking (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.808388, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rvent l\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.808487, "o", "## Prioritised Remediation Steps & Verification\r\n"]
[231.808538, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.808613, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[231.80863, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rO"]
[231.808718, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.808872, "o", "### Phase 1: Immediate Network Isolation & Perimeter Blocking\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.808937, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.809003, "o", "1. **Block Attacker IP & C2 Infrastructure**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.809035, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.809267, "o", "   - Apply boundary firewall rule to drop inbound and outbound traffic to/from `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.809338, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.809701, "o", "   - Add DNS sinkhole / block rules for C2 domain `update-rdp.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:9`) and mining pool host `xmr.rdp.evil` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:4`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.809873, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.809939, "o", "   - **Verification**: Test DNS resolution and ping to `198.51.100.92` and verify dropped packets in firewall logs."]
[231.809976, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.810009, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.810064, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.810162, "o", "2. **Isolate Compromised Host**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[231.810205, "o", "> "]
[231.810469, "o", "   - Isolate `rdp-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) from the local production VLAN while maintaining out-of-band management access for security responders. \r"]
[231.810548, "o", "\u001bM\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[C\u001b[K.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.810683, "o", "### Phase 2: RDP Hardening & Credential Protection\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.810787, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> 1. **Enforce Network Level Authentication (NLA)**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.810837, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.811119, "o", "   - Configure registry key `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp`: set `UserAuthentication` to `1` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.811168, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.811637, "o", "   - Enforce via Group Policy Object (GPO): *Computer Configuration -> Administrative Templates -> Windows Components -> Remote Desktop Services -> Remote Desktop Session Host -> Security -> Require user authentication for remote connections by using Network Level Authentication*.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.811858, "o", "   - **Verification**: Execute `Get-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp' -Name UserAuthentication` and confirm value is `1`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.81195, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[231.811967, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.812048, "o", "2. **Credential Reset & Account Lockout Enforcement**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.812129, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.812367, "o", "   - Reset passwords for all administrative accounts (including `Administrator` and `svc-backup`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security-events.csv:3`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.812531, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.812694, "o", "   - Configure Account Lockout Policy (e.g. threshold = 5 failed attempts) to prevent brute-force attacks (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.812793, "o", "### Phase 3: Artifact Quarantine & Persistence Neutralization\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.812915, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.813019, "o", "Per rules, artifacts must be **quarantined/backed up** rather than immediately deleted.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.813105, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.813227, "o", "1. **Quarantine Ransomware Payload (`C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe`)**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.813284, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.813611, "o", "   - Action: Move `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe:1`) to secure forensic quarantine folder `C:\\ProgramData\\Quarantine\\` and restrict ACLs.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.813722, "o", "   - **Verification**: Confirm file is removed from `C:\\Users\\Public\\` and hashed.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.813794, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.813911, "o", "2. **Disable & Remove Scheduled Task (`UpdateHelper`)**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.813972, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.814261, "o", "   - Action: Export task XML to quarantine backup, then run `schtasks /Change /TN \"UpdateHelper\" /Disable` and `schtasks /Delete /TN \"UpdateHelper\" /F` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.814358, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.81453, "o", "   - **Verification**: Run `schtasks /Query /TN \"UpdateHelper\"` and confirm task is not found.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.814635, "o", "3. **Disable & Quarantine Malicious Service (`svc-helper`)**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.814663, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.815179, "o", "   - Action: Stop service `sc stop svc-helper`, set startup type to disabled `sc config svc-helper start= disabled`, backup service configuration, and move `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys:1`) to quarantine. Delete service registry key `sc delete svc-helper`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.815272, "o", "   - **Verification**: Run `Get-Service -Name \"svc-helper\"` and confirm service is absent.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.815357, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.815373, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.815489, "o", "4. **Remove Silent Registry Run Key (`svc`)**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.815784, "o", "   - Action: Export registry key backup, then remove value `svc` from `HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[231.81589, "o", "> "]
[231.81604, "o", "   - **Verification**: Execute `Get-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run' -Name svc` and verify key does not exist.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[231.81614, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.816159, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.816252, "o", "### Phase 4: Forensic Logging & Tamper-Resistant Monitoring\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.81636, "o", "1. **Configure Centralized Log Forwarding**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.816674, "o", "   - Implement Windows Event Forwarding (WEF) or Syslog agent streaming Security, System, and Application logs directly to a central SIEM (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.816765, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.816945, "o", "   - Enable auditing for EventID 1102 (Log Clearance) and alert SOC immediately upon log clearing events (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx:2`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.817038, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[231.817147, "o", "   - **Verification**: Generate test event log entry and confirm receipt at SIEM receiver.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[231.817233, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
